  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "Suppose that \\(P = 2^m\\) and \\(Q = 3^n.\\) Which of the following is equal to \\(12^{mn}\\) for every pair of integers \\((m, n)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(P^2 Q\\)",
    "B": "\\(P^n Q^m\\)",
    "C": "\\(P^n Q^{2m}\\)",
    "D": "\\(P^{2m} Q^n\\)",
    "E": "\\(P^{2n} Q^m\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Since \\(P\\) and \\(Q\\) use bases \\(2\\) and \\(3\\), factor \\(12\\) as \\(2^2\\cdot3\\). The power rules then give\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n12^{mn}\n&=2^{2mn}3^{mn}\\\\\n&=(2^m)^{2n}(3^n)^m\\\\\n&=P^{2n}Q^m.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nEvery base here is positive. Zero exponents give \\(1\\), and negative exponents mean reciprocals of nonzero quantities, so these steps remain valid for every pair of integers \\((m,n)\\).\n\nThe answer is \\(P^{2n}Q^m\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
